[ti:97. A Small Blue Case]
[by:Generated by iChochy]

[00:00.672]Lesson 97. | 第97课。
[00:04.292]I left a suitcase on the train to London the other day. | 前几天我把一个手提箱忘在了去伦敦的火车上。
[00:08.572]Can you describe /dɪˈskraɪb/ it, sir? | 您能描述一下它吗，先生？
[00:10.592]It's a small /smɔːl/ blue case /keɪs/ and it's got a zip /zɪp/. | 它是一个小的蓝色箱子，上面有拉链。
[00:15.022]There's a label /ˈleɪbl/ on the handle /ˈhændl/ with my name and address /əˈdres/ on it. | 把手上有一个标签，上面有我的姓名和地址。
[00:20.262]Is this case /keɪs/ yours? | 这个箱子是您的吗？
[00:21.822]No, that's not mine. | 不，那不是我的。
[00:25.102]What about this one? | 这个呢？
[00:27.052]This one's got a label /ˈleɪbl/. | 这个上面有标签。
[00:28.902]Let me see it. | 让我看看。
[00:31.702]What's your name and address /əˈdres/? | 您的姓名和地址是什么？
[00:33.842]David Hall, 83 Bridge Street. | 大卫·霍尔，布里奇街83号。
[00:37.472]That's right. | 对了。
[00:38.902]D N Hall, 83 Bridge Street. | D. N. 霍尔，布里奇街83号。
[00:44.252]Five shillings /ˈʃɪlɪŋz/, please. | 请付五先令。
[00:45.742]Here you are. | 给你。
[00:46.812]Thank you. | 谢谢。
[00:49.022]Hey! | 嘿！
[00:50.052]What's the matter? | 怎么了？
[00:51.482]This case /keɪs/ doesn't belong /bɪˈlɒŋ/ to me. | 这个箱子不是我的。
[00:54.672]You've given me the wrong /rɒŋ/ case /keɪs/. | 你给我拿错了箱子。
